  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">St&#xf6;d fredsbyggande datainsamling UNDP DRK</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support for peacebuilding data UNDP DRC - Support for peacebuilding data</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Insatsen &#xe4;r ett st&#xf6;d till UNDP f&#xf6;r fortsatt arbete med datainsamling i &#xf6;stra DRK i syfte att tillhandah&#xe5;lla ett unikt rigor&#xf6;st, kontinuerligt och detaljerat dataset f&#xf6;r att st&#xf6;dja programarbete samt uppf&#xf6;ljning och utv&#xe4;rdering av framsteg mot fred, r&#xe4;ttvisa och s&#xe4;kerhet i DR Kongo. Detta &#xe4;r projektets andra fas, d&#xe4;r den f&#xf6;rsta fasen p&#xe5;gick fram till juni 2017. 
 
Verksamheten kommer inledningsvis att fokusera p&#xe5; samma geografiska omr&#xe5;den som projektets f&#xf6;rsta fas (Nord- och Sydkivu samt Ituri-provinsen), som fortfarande &#xe4;r mycket utsatta omr&#xe5;den trots stora investeringar gjorda av det internationella samfundet. Denna andra fas kommer dock ocks&#xe5; att g&#xf6;ra det m&#xf6;jligt f&#xf6;r FN och dess partner att reagera snabbare p&#xe5; tidiga varningar och kan utvidgas till andra delar av landet f&#xf6;r att, genom tillf&#xf6;rlitliga data och analyser, st&#xf6;dja &#xe5;tg&#xe4;rder f&#xf6;r att f&#xf6;rebygga potentiella konflikter och eskaleringar av v&#xe5;ld som liknar de som nyligen sett i Kasai och Tanganyika.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The contribution is a support to UNDP for continued work on data collection in eastern DRC in order to provide a unique, rigorous, continuous and detailed dataset to support program work as well as follow-up and evaluation of progress towards peace, justice and security in DR Congo. This is the second phase of the project, where the first phase ends in June 2017.

Polling will focus on the same geographic areas as the first phase of the project (North and South Kivu and Ituri Province), which are still highly exposed areas despite major investments made by the international community. However, this second phase will also allow the UN and its partners to respond faster to early warning and expand to other parts of the country to support, through reliable data and analysis, measures to prevent potential conflicts and escalations of violence such as similar to those recently seen in Kasai and Tanganyika.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The objective of the project is to: Contribute to sustainability of peace in the DRC and strengthen peace-building and reconstruction efforts undertaken by the Government and its partners, including the United Nations system, through the collection of accurate and reliable data in order to contribute to better formulation of policies and programs on security, justice and stabilization.</narrative>
  </description>
